[00:02.17] (Steve Katz)
[00:17.39] Sometimes in Winter
[00:21.60] I gaze into the streets
[00:24.21] And walk through snow and city sleet
[00:27.02] Behind your room
[00:36.02] Sometimes in Winter
[00:40.01] Forgotten memories
[00:42.99] Remember you behind the trees
[00:46.06] With leaves that cried
[00:56.66] By the window once I waited for you
[00:59.24] Laughing slightly you would run
[01:02.91] Trees alone would shield us in the meadow
[01:05.47] Makin' love in the evening sun
[01:21.71] Now you're gone girl
[01:26.72] And the lamp posts call your name
[01:29.94] I can hear, them
[01:32.64] In the spring of frozen rain
[01:35.71] Now you're gone girl
[01:38.65] And the time's slowed down till dawn
[01:41.68] It's a cold room and the walls ask
[01:45.73] Where you've gone
